recorded 2026-11-14 9.0.10 neutralized
The T061 recording of StartCLI trace --reset on a non-production 9.0.10 node with the 9.0.10 client on JDK 21, run right after the set_ok recording: exit 0, stdout only the 9.0 client preamble (the JAVA_HOME line, the hostname verification warning, the client's own log record "ERROR <time> [main      ] DnsServerAddressStreamProviders Unable to load io.netty.resolver.dns.macos.MacOSDnsServerAddressStreamProvider, fallback to system defaults. …", the hostname verification warning again, the password prompt, the hostname verification warning again, two empty lines), stderr only the JVM notice about JAVA_TOOL_OPTIONS. There is no confirmation line: as on 8.1, StartCLI prints no n-OK line for the CommandResult("OK") of this form. The reset names no logger, and no logger name appears in the output. The netty log record is kept verbatim; it names no host. Neutralized as in research D-26: the trust-store path in the JAVA_TOOL_OPTIONS notice is replaced by /home/jdoe/.config/inubit-mcp/acme-truststore.p12; the output names no host.
